   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. Presence of approved, funded policy/strategy/plan for adaptation to the adverse impacts of climate resilience and low greenhouse gas emissions development in a manner that does not threaten food production  (13.2.1)
3.2. 15% degree of integrated water resource management implementation (scale 0-100) (6.5.1)
3.3. National and local disaster risk reduction strategies adopted and financed and proportion of local governments that adopt and implement local disaster risk reduction strategies in line with Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030 (11.b.1, 11b.2)
3.4: 10.5% Coverage by protected areas of important sites for mountain biodiversity (15.4.1)
3.5 Water 100%; Sanitation 38% Proportion of local administrative units with established and operational policies and procedures for participation of local communities in water and sanitation management (6.b.1)
3.6. 10% Renewable energy share in the total final energy consumption (7.2.1) 
3.7. Progress towards sustainable forest management (15.2.1)</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. There is no approved, funded policy/strategy/plan for adaptation to the adverse impacts of climate resilience and low greenhouse gas emissions development in a manner that does not threaten food production (13.2.1)
3.2. 6% of integrated water resource management implementation (scale 0-100) (6.5.1)
3.3. There is no national and local disaster risk reduction strategies adopted and financed and proportion of local governments that adopt and implement local disaster risk reduction strategies in line with Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030 (11.b.1, 11b.2)

3.4. 6.2% Coverage by protected areas of important sites for mountain biodiversity (15.4.1)

3.5. Water 89,1%; Sanitation 28,6% Proportion of local administrative units with established and operational policies and procedures for participation of local communities in water and sanitation management (6.b.1)

3.6. 2,1% renewable energy share in the total final energy consumption (7.2.1) 

3.7. There has been no progress towards sustainable forest management (15.2.1)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1: UNDP-GCF Project on National Adaptation Planning is launched. Enhanced NDC is submitted to the UNFCCC (IRRF 5.2.2); 
3.2.1: Natural Disasters Data Management Center is benefiting local communities living in disaster prone areas; 
3.4.1: A project concept on establishment of protected areas in the Southern Kyrgyzstan is developed and submitted to GEF7 (15.4.1);
3.2.3. SAP has been finalized and endorsed by countries of Kyrgyzstan and Kazakhstan (6.5.1)
3.6. IRENAs RRA has been finalized and issued to promote the use of solar and wind energy (7.2.1)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1. UNDP-GCF roject on National Adaptation Planning was launched in October 2021. NDC was endorsed on 24.09.2021 by decision of the Coordination Council on Environment, Climate Chnage and Green Economy and submitted to UNFCCC Secretariat (IRRF 5.2.2);
3.2.1. Natural Disasters Data Management Center was strengthened to respond to the urgent demand related to COVID-19.
3.4.1: A project concept on establishment of protected areas in the Southern Kyrgyzstan was developed and to be submitted to GEF7 (15.4.1) 
3.2.3. SAP was endorsed by countries of Kyrgyzstan and Kazakhstan (6.5.1)
3.6. IRENAs RRA was discussed with national partners and the road map of solar and wind energy deployment has been prepared (7.2.1)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1: GCF Project on National Adaptation Plan is launched. NDC update/enhancement is finalized and updated NDC is submitted to the UNFCCC (IRRF 5.2.2); 
3.1.2: Coal to Gas in Schools of Bishkek and E-mobility and heating systems for new settlements around the Bishkek city ;
3.2.3. CTWC is supported with the re-engineering of the draft SAP and SAP is endorsed by the Country (6.5.1)
3.6. A project concept is developed to increase the share of RES in the energy production for provision of sustainable and clean energy to new settlements (7.2.1)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1: UNDP-GCF Project on National Adaptation Planning was approved by the LPAC and is under inception. Due to the COVID-19 crisis the deadlines for submission of the enhanced NDC targets have been postponed to March 2021. The work is in progress in close partnership with the national partners and the updated NDC will be submitted to the UNFCCC in March 2021 (IRRF 5.2.2); 
3.1.2: In coordination with the Bishkek City Hall a Project Proposal was developed on Coal to Gas conversion of 18 Bishkek Municipal Schools with confirmed co-financing from the municipal budget. The activity was financially supported by the Russian Knowledge Management Project and the Russian expert was sourced from the Experts Ondemand Platform. The concept was submitted to the call for proposals of the UNDP - Russia Trust Fund for development, but it was not approved for funding at this time and UNDP in collaboration with the State partners is looking into alternative funding opportunities to implement the plans. Feasibility study for promotion of E-mobility was initiated;
3.2.3. UNDP has got funding from the SIWI to support the CTWC with the re-engineering of the SAP into basin plans and the project is under implementation in two countries with UNDP Astana as a leading CO (6.5.1)
3.6. Under the efforts of enhancing the countrys NDC ambitions, UNDP has engaged with IRENA which has initiated a Renewables readiness Assessment with focus on solar and wind energy. The results will be made available in 2021 and this would open up new opportunities and investments for the country to promote and increase the share of renewables in its energy production and consumption towards sustainable energy for all and reaching full energy independence. (7.2.1)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2 gender sensitive National Adaptation and Low-Carbon Development strategic documents are in place</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">to be reported at the end of 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
